{
    "name": "WES tertiary analysis from FASTQ (v1)",
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "format-version": "0.1",
    "annotation": "Germline whole exome sequencing (WES) analysis from paired-end FASTQ to a prioritised, annotated variant table.\n\nRuns once per sample of a list:paired collection (element identifiers are used as sample names):\n\n1. Read QC (FastQC) and adapter/quality trimming (fastp).\n2. Alignment to the reference with BWA-MEM (read groups set from the sample name), duplicate marking\n   (Picard MarkDuplicates) and alignment statistics (samtools stats).\n3. Exome capture QC: Picard CollectHsMetrics (on-target rate, fold-80, % target bases >= 20x), per-target\n   coverage with mosdepth (bases at 1/10/20/30/50x per target, for gap analysis) and per-gene coverage of the\n   coding exons (mosdepth over the coding-region BED).\n4. Germline variant calling with FreeBayes (standard input filters: MAPQ >= 30, BQ >= 20), and copy-number calls\n   (deletions, duplications, chromosome dosage) from each sample's target read depth against the other samples of\n   the run and an optional reference panel of the same kit (needs at least 3 other samples).\n5. Tertiary analysis, the embedded \"WES tertiary analysis from VCF (v2)\" workflow: normalisation, restriction\n   to the padded targets, quality filtering, ClinVar + gnomAD + SnpEff annotation, prioritisation and tables,\n   runs of homozygosity, and the clinical interpretation report (diagnostic, candidate, ACMG secondary,\n   carrier, pharmacogenomic and risk-allele findings, with read depth and coverage from this workflow).\n6. One MultiQC report for all samples (FastQC, fastp, Picard, samtools, bcftools stats, SnpEff).\n\nReference FASTA, target BED, ClinVar and gnomAD must use the same genome build and chromosome naming.\n",
    "tags": [
        "WES",
        "exome",
        "germline",
        "variant-calling",
        "variant-annotation",
        "variant-prioritization",
        "tertiary-analysis"
    ],
    "license": "MIT",
    "release": "0.10",
    "uuid": "e4cd5a16-74be-4629-a676-4542c043ea15",
    "comments": [],
